{
  "about": [
    "The cases of the subtitle rule of plan 90, which two programs apply.",
    "media-operator's command sidecar chooses the track that mpv shows,",
    "and library-operator's media browser marks that track on a movie's",
    "page. subtitletracks_test.go in media-operator and rule.rs in",
    "library-operator/media-browser both read this file, so a change to",
    "either rule fails a test until the two agree.",
    "",
    "A track is one entry of mpv's track-list. An embedded track gives",
    "its language tag, its title, and its flags. An external track gives",
    "the name of its file beside a video named Movie (2024).mkv, and the",
    "language and flags that mpv reads from that name. events is the",
    "event count that library-operator records, and an absent count is",
    "not a count of zero. Each track's mpv id is its position in the list,",
    "from 1.",
    "",
    "The files are from a survey of a home cluster's catalog, reduced to",
    "the English tracks' flags, titles, and event counts. A case names",
    "one of them, or lists its own tracks.",
    "",
    "want in a choose case is the mpv id of the chosen track, 0 for no",
    "subtitles, and -1 for a case in which the rule sets nothing and",
    "mpv's own choice stands."
  ],
